{
  "timestamp": "2026-08-12T18:23:18Z",
  "title": "The Puzzle School rebuilt as an Astro site on codeyam-cms",
  "type": "feature",
  "userRequest": "Ok sounds good. Let's resume",
  "description": "Rebuilt the site as a static Astro app consuming @codeyam/cms, replacing the Next.js placeholder. Three pages — Home, About and Contact — render entirely from markdown in a `pages` content collection, including the home page, so a page created in /admin goes live with no code change via the [...slug] catch-all the CMS demo site lacks. The design's six line structures (Fibonacci spiral, sine field, Koch fragment, dragon curve, branching tree, morse rule) are generated from their mathematical rules in src/lib/structures.ts rather than pasted as path data, so each one's deliberate incompleteness stays a named parameter; the tree's irregularity comes from a seeded PRNG so the static build stays byte-reproducible. Fixed four defects found along the way: @codeyam/cms's integrate CLI was a silent no-op for every consumer (entry guard compared import.meta.url against a non-realpath'd argv[1]); the seed adapter serialised nested content as [object Object]; site settings were frozen until a dev-server restart; and codeyam's capture pipeline flattened every SVG transform. That last fix had to be reverted to pass the audit since it lives in a generated file — see the queued plan `recapture-svg-screenshots-after-the-upstream-capture-fix`, and note the 22 component screenshots in this commit show flattened SVG geometry until it runs.",
